            "copy": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>In 2001, Bradley Bennett started making his spicy blend of pickles for friends and family from his kitchen in Santa Barbara, California. The recipe was simple: peak-season produce, bold California flavors, and a brine that had been dialed in to perfection.</p><p>Friends kept asking for more. Then friends of friends. Then people at the farmers market. Then stores. The demand was undeniable — these weren't just pickles. They were the pickles people had been looking for their whole lives.</p><p>Bradley created Pacific Pickle Works so that everyone could enjoy them. The jars still leave Santa Barbara. The brine is still made the same way. The only thing that's changed is the scale — and even that, we've kept as small as we can.</p>",
